the u.s. is expected to send a plane to  Japan to bring back the American  passengers from a cruise ship that was  quarantined due to the corona virus the  number of confirmed coronavirus cases is  now more than 49,000 worldwide including  15 cases here in the US the outbreak has  led to more than 1500 deaths in China  alone  Deborah pata is in Hong Kong with more  on the plan to evacuate the Americans  good morning we're learning that at  least 380 Americans and their families  will be evacuated from the diamond  princess I spoke to one of the  passengers who told me she received an  email from the American Embassy in Japan  offering her a seat on a US chartered  plane leaving tomorrow the diamonds  princess has been in Yokohama for well  over a week now the most common ailment  on board appears to be boredom  passengers have been confined to their  cabins with only the occasional stroll  allowed on the deck in Wuhan China where  the epidemic started social media  postings show ongoing draconian measures  by the Chinese government to contain the  virus the front door the family  suspected of being infected is welded  shut  emergency workers spray disinfectant  inside offices as workers just sit at  their computers and yellow body bags are  still being removed from homes and  hospitals outside of China the diamond  princess is the site of the biggest art  break with its over two hundred and  fiction's including more than a dozen  Americans on Sunday Americans on board  the ship wishing to be evacuated will be  taken by bus to a u.s. chartered plane  but before boarding they will undergo a  health screening symptomatic passengers  may not be allowed to fly for CBS this  morning Saturday I'm Debora patta  in Hong Kong  you
 

